The '''reality vision''' is a joke [[helmet]] in [[1.RV-Pre1]].

== Obtaining ==
=== Mob loot ===
[[Zombie]]s, [[Zombie Villager (old)|zombie villager]]s, [[skeleton]]s, [[creeper]]s, and [[endermen]] can spawn with reality vision on their head. They have a chance{{More info|what is the chance? is it 8% like armor? is it affected by looting?}} to drop it when killed by the player.

== Usage ==
=== Player ===
Reality vision is equipped via the [[helmet]] slot. When equipped, it shows a {{w|minimap}} in the bottom-center of the screen (which moves when the [[player]]'s camera moves). The minimap shows all [[chunk]]s that were currently rendered. The player's location is represented by a light green [[beacon]] beam marker on the map.

The reality vision displays a vision overlay when worn, similar to the [[Carved Pumpkin|carved pumpkin]] overlay. Unlike the carved pumpkin overlay, it can not be disabled by pressing {{key|F1}} and can only be disabled by going into [[third-person view]]. The overlay is called <code>cantseeshit<!-- Do not change this; this is that word that is actually used-->captain.png</code> in the assets folder.

The reality vision activates a [[shader]] when equipped (<code>scan_pincushion</code>), which makes the screen appear like an old {{w|television}} screen. This shader can be toggled by pressing {{key|F4}}, it is also automatically activated when going from first person to third person. 

[[Sign]]s use the texture with the text "OBEY" while reality vision is equipped, a reference to the movie ''{{w|They Live}}''.

=== Mobs ===
Mobs wearing reality vision are nearly passive to the player. Undead mobs do not burn in sunlight when wearing reality vision, since reality vision counts as a helmet.

Creepers wearing reality vision completely ignore the player, [[ocelot]]s and [[snow golem]]s. They can still be lit with [[flint and steel]], however.

Zombies and zombie villagers wearing reality vision do not attack the player normally, but still attack [[Villager (old)|villager]]s. However, zombies without reality vision could "call" zombies with reality vision to attack the player, tamed [[wolves]], snow golems and [[iron golem]]s.

Endermen wearing reality vision do not attack the player when hit, but are still angered when looked at without a pumpkin.

Skeletons wearing reality vision are completely passive.

